    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, we are leaning heavily into speed and favorable matchups against weak arms to maintain our Roto momentum. **Corbin Carroll** (80.77) headlines our lineup as our strongest play; while the platoon split against Abbott is traditionally suboptimal, the massive SP_xERA of 5.01 and **Carroll**'s elite sprint profile make him a must-start at the top of the order. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) is positioned for a high-floor performance against Waguespack, benefitting from a substantial 14% boost due to the R-on-R platoon alignment, making him our anchor at 1B. **Gabriel Moreno** also earns a strong recommendation (66.77) as he draws a soft matchup against Abbott, where his recent hot streak and favorable batting order placement provide the highest efficiency of our available battery options.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Isaac Paredes** (45.78), who barely missed the cut for the final UTIL spot. While **Paredes** offers a solid base, he was squeezed out by the efficiency profiles of **Jose Caballero** and **Seiya Suzuki**; despite **Caballero** drawing a lower score due to an unfavorable lineup spot, his capacity for game-changing stolen bases remains a priority over the static production of our bench options. We are closely monitoring the lineup status for **Austin Riley** (48.83); if he is bumped from the #8 hole or if late-breaking weather reports shift, we have the flexibility to pivot. We are also wary of **Mickey Moniak** (55.59); while his park factor is a massive +14%, he faces a significant 15% penalty due to the platoon disadvantage against Griffin, though we are banking on his ability to capitalize on the pitcher's slow delivery to bolster our SB totals. \n\nFinally, managers should keep a sharp eye on the **Max Muncy** (57.10) and **Henry Bolte** (60.79) matchup against Javier. Both possess high-variance outcomes given Javier's high xERA, but their exposure to a pitcher with a 5.16 xERA makes them high-upside plays despite the negative park factors in play. We continue to hold **James Wood** on the IL, as he remains unavailable, while bench depth players like **Griffin Conine** and **Cole Young** remain ready but ultimately lack the projected daily efficiency required to displace our current starters in this high-leverage environment.",
